; TechTraining.inix -- how this database opens, and how its table is heard.
;
; ABOUT 1,170 FREE PRESENTATIONS on technology and accessibility, from the Tech
; Training directory by Jamal Mazrui: webinars, demonstrations, podcasts and
; workshops from 25 sources, in 20 topic categories, each with its year, length,
; description, presenter, series and source.
;
; PLAY ONE. Play Stream (Alt+Shift+P) plays the presentation itself in the Homer
; Player: an audio file directly, a video on YouTube or the like through yt-dlp.
; Mark several (Space) and Alt+Shift+P plays them all, as a play list. Three short
; ones come marked, to show how. A presentation whose medium is "page" lives on a
; web page instead: Control+Enter on its url opens it in your browser. Control+Enter
; on source_url opens the publisher's page, and resources lists any slides,
; transcripts or handouts.
;
; FIND ONE. The row speaks title, minutes and medium: what it is, how long it
; takes, and whether Alt+Shift+P plays it. category, source and series are pick
; lists, so filtering on one offers its values, and each category comes with the
; directory's own one-sentence definition. Quick-Lessons lists the playable ones of
; fifteen minutes or less; Newest lists those from this year and last; the
; listening_list report writes up the marked ones, to keep or print.
;
; scripts\makeTechTraining in DbDo's development folder rebuilds this file from
; the directory.
;
; [Database] decides which table the window starts on. [Table:<name>] decides which
; fields the row speaks, in what order, and how the rows are sorted. DbDo writes
; these keys back whenever you change the columns, the sort or the filter.

[Database]

InitialTable = presentations

[Table:lookups]

SelectFields = fld, val
OrderFields = fld, ordinal
WhereFilter =

[Table:maps]

SelectFields = kind, prime1, prime2
OrderFields = kind, prime1
WhereFilter =

[Table:presentations]

SelectFields = title, minutes, medium
; OrderFields, 13 October 2026: newest first, since recent presentations match the software people use now.
OrderFields = year DESC, title
WhereFilter =
